kspalaiologos/bzip3, release 1.5.4, plus one local change.
Upstream: https://github.com/kspalaiologos/bzip3

libbz3.h, common.h and libsais.h are byte-identical to 1.5.4.
libbz3.c is 1.5.4 with one change, inside bz3_compress and
bz3_decompress, the only bzip3 entry points karyozip calls: the
independent blocks are encoded and decoded side by side under OpenMP,
each with its own state, and written in order, so the bytes are the
same. Diffed against 1.5.4 on 2026-10-19: no other line differs.

1.5.4 took the two fixes this tree carried against 1.5.3, with the same
lines: the last block's size in bz3_compress (#175; 1.5.3 lost half the
data on an input that is an exact multiple of the block size) and the
bz3_bound check in bz3_decompress (#174). lastblock_check.c still
reproduces the first; on this tree it must print all bytes back:

  gcc -O2 -DVERSION='"x"' -Ibzip3 -o lbc bzip3/lastblock_check.c \
      bzip3/libbz3.c -lpthread && ./lbc
